          "title": "You'll want to know: கிண்டல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கிண்டல் — kiṇṭal — \"teasing; mockery\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "என் தம்பி என் சமையலைக் கிண்டல் செய்தான். eṉ tampi eṉ camaiyalaik kiṇṭal ceytāṉ. My younger brother made fun of my cooking."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கிண்டல் (kiṇṭal) செய், to tease."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கிண்டல் (kiṇṭal) is native Dravidian, from கிண்டு kiṇṭu, \"to poke, to stir\" (DEDR 1542); the entry gives கிண்டல் as stirring up mischief."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
